# gts9uwifi additions - append to arch/arm64/configs/halium.config
# S-Pen (Wacom WEZ01) - drivers/input/wacom; requires Kconfig/Makefile wiring
# (drivers/input/Kconfig sources neither wacom nor sec_input - mirror the
#  mechanism that includes sec_input, or add:
#    drivers/input/Kconfig:  source "drivers/input/wacom/Kconfig"
#    drivers/input/Makefile: obj-$(CONFIG_EPEN_WACOM_WEZ01) += wacom/ )
CONFIG_EPEN_WACOM_WEZ01=m
# Ultra touch: goodix_ts_berlin (import source from SM-X910 OSRC drop;
# ships as vendor_dlkm module goodix_ts_berlin.ko on stock - config symbol
# per imported Kconfig, expected CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_GOODIX_BERLIN=m)
# WLAN: Ultra is WCN785x "kiwi" (stock module qca_cld3_kiwi_v2.ko), not
# qca6490 - deviceinfo_kernel_wlan_chip="kiwi_v2" set. Verify the imported
# qcacld-3.0 tree carries the kiwi_v2 profile; if not, take it from the
# X910 OSRC wlan tree. cnss2 platform driver supports both families.
# PROJECT_NAME: audio-kernel and camera-kernel key per-board Samsung configs
# on PROJECT_NAME=$deviceinfo_codename (=gts9uwifi) - import the gts9u*
# config/sensor-set files from the X910 OSRC audio-kernel and camera-kernel
# trees (this is where the Ultra's five camera sensors are wired kernel-side).
